 "result_text": "`get_schema` no longer crashes when the device's `<data>` element isn't in the `ietf-netconf-monitoring` namespace, as with Junos. The change is in `GetSchemaReply._parsing_hook` in `ncclient/operations/retrieve.py`.\n\nIt still looks for `<data>` in the `ietf-netconf-monitoring` namespace first. If that finds nothing, it tries the base NETCONF namespace, then `<data>` in any namespace, then `<data>` with no namespace. If none match, the schema data is set to `None` instead of raising the `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'text'` error.\n\nI tested it with a made-up reply whose `<data>` sits in an unrelated namespace, and it returned the text. I didn't run it against the real Junos reply from the gist or run the existing test suite.",
